v4: split-tender + tips + mid-shift cash + receipt reprint + push

Backend
-------
- New CashMovement model + 4-type enum (drop / add / payout / payin)
  with shiftId + recordedById + reason + optional manager-override PIN.
- New ExpoPushToken model — unique on (userId, token), tracked by
  device + locationId so admin can target "all tablets at Gulberg".
- Migration 20260511040000_v4_cash_movements_push — idempotent
  (IF NOT EXISTS + DO NOTHING on enum dup).
- /pos/shifts/:id/cash-movements (POST + GET).
- /pos/orders/:id/receipt-data (JSON, mirrors the existing HTML
  /pos/receipt/:orderId so the tablet thermal printer can fetch
  structured data instead of parsing HTML).
- getZReport extended with per-tender breakdown, cash-movement
  aggregates, tipsCents from Order.tipCents, and tablet-friendly
  field names (grossCents / netCents / byMethod / cashMovements /
  expectedCashCents / varianceCents). Original field names kept
  for back-compat with existing admin pages.
- New /notifications module with /register (POST) + /register (DELETE)
  for Expo push tokens. Upsert-by-(userId, token) so re-registers
  don't bloat the table.

Tablet
------
- POS tender screen rewritten:
  - Tip selector (none / 10% / 15% / 20%) computed off subtotal,
    passed to /pos/orders as tipCents.
  - Split-tender: add multiple tender rows (any mix of cash / card /
    jazzcash / easypaisa); each row tracks amountCents + tenderedCents
    (cash overage = change owed). "EXACT" button on the cash keypad
    fills the remaining balance. Fire is gated on fullyPaid.
  - Backend payment call sends the full tenders array — multi-row
    Payment creation already supported by /pos/payments.
- Receipt fetch URL fixed (/pos/orders/:id/receipt-data, not the
  non-existent /orders/:id/receipt).
- Shift home gets a "Cash movement" button → opens new
  CashMovementModal (drop / add / payout / payin with keypad +
  reason). Movements list rendered inline with +/- coloring.
- Active-orders gets a 🧾 Reprint button per order (calls
  printReceipt(orderId) — same code path as tender-time print).
- Z-report types in shift home aligned with the new backend response
  shape (cashMovements block + tablet-friendly aliases).

